\textbf{\text{ID-GEN}\xspace Base case (step 1):} 


















Let, at any recursion level of \text{ID-GEN}\xspace, the input dataset $\mathcal{D}[{\hat{\mathbf{X}}}, \mathbf{V}]$ is sampled from a specific joint distribution $P({\hat{\mathbf{X}}},\mathbf{V})$, i.e., $\mathcal{D}[{\hat{\mathbf{X}}}, \mathbf{V}] \sim P({\hat{\mathbf{X}}},\mathbf{V})$ where ${\hat{\mathbf{X}}}$ is the set of intervened variables at step 7s. Given a target interventional query $P(\mathbf{y})$ over a causal graph $G=(V, E)$,  suppose \text{ID-GEN}\xspace$(\mathbf{Y}, \mathbf{X}= \emptyset, G, \mathcal{D}, {\hat{\mathbf{X}}}, {\hat{{G}}})$ enters step 1 and returns $\mathcal{H}$.
Then $\mathcal{H}$ is a valid sampling network for $P(\mathbf{y})$  with fixed consistent ${\hat{\mathbf{X}}}= {\hat{\mathbf{x}}}$.

